OCR Check Android sample

Model: MiniCPM-OCR-Jev by OpenBMB (https://huggingface.co/openbmb/MiniCPM-OCR-Jev, revision
a0ed278eb6aa1f333a711665ab610055a4a816ab), licensed under Apache License 2.0, trained from
Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B (Apache License 2.0). The LiteRT graphs, the tables and the tokenizer.json the app
loads are converted or copied from that checkpoint, published in
https://huggingface.co/litert-community/MiniCPM-OCR-Decision-2B-LiteRT and copied to the phone by
install_to_device.sh; they are not part of this source tree.

app/src/main/java/com/google/ai/edge/examples/ocr_verification/HostMath.kt and Verifier.kt port the
Python host of litert-community/MiniCPM-OCR-Decision-2B-LiteRT (host/decide_host, revision
672db2e312814fd9b56aa02d494755676140cfdb, Apache License 2.0), which follows the score path of
scripts/minicpm-ocr-jev/eval/score.py of github.com/OpenBMB/MiniCPM-OCR (commit
8177040f0d6c824ccf87bc18b938b6a0f91b6d0e, Apache License 2.0, licenses/MiniCPM-OCR-APACHE-2.0.txt):
the prompt and its token checks; the picture preprocessing, position tables and rotary tables of
Hugging Face transformers (Apache License 2.0, licenses/Transformers-APACHE-2.0.txt); and PyTorch's
uint8 antialiased bicubic resize (BSD 3-Clause License, licenses/PyTorch-BSD-3-Clause.txt).

app/src/main/java/com/google/ai/edge/examples/ocr_verification/RenderPage.kt ports the page of the
source's renderer, scripts/minicpm-ocr-jev/renderer/render_module/render_label.py of
github.com/OpenBMB/MiniCPM-OCR at the commit above (Apache License 2.0): the pass that protects the
math spans, the HTML path for tables, the page's CSS and its layout scripts (the table layout script
is copied as it is). Its Markdown step writes the HTML that Python-Markdown 3.10.3 writes for the
syntax it covers (BSD 3-Clause License, licenses/Python-Markdown-BSD-3-Clause.txt). Changes: the
page loads the bundled DejaVu Sans before the source's font list, and the WebView draws it in place
of the source's Chromium.

app/src/main/java/com/google/ai/edge/examples/ocr_verification/QwenBpeTokenizer.kt follows the
published tokenizer.json contract of Hugging Face tokenizers and transformers (Apache License 2.0;
licenses/Tokenizers-APACHE-2.0.txt and licenses/Transformers-APACHE-2.0.txt): added-token
extraction, NFC, the Split pre-tokenizer regex, the ByteLevel mapping and byte-level BPE.

app/src/main/assets/render/katex/ holds KaTeX 0.16.47 (katex.min.js, katex.min.css and its fonts),
Copyright (c) 2013-2020 Khan Academy and other contributors, MIT License (licenses/KaTeX-MIT.txt).
app/src/main/assets/render/fonts/ holds DejaVuSans.ttf and DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf of the DejaVu fonts
2.37 (licenses/DejaVu-Fonts-LICENSE.txt).

The text recognizer is ML Kit Text Recognition v2 (com.google.mlkit:text-recognition, the model
bundled in the app), used under the ML Kit terms (https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/terms).

The example pages app/src/main/assets/examples/*.png were drawn for this sample (English text
written for it: the invoice set in DejaVu Sans Condensed with a made-up shop, items and prices, scaled down to a quarter and back up like a low-resolution scan; the formula sheet set in DejaVu Serif). app/src/test/resources/render_html_public.json holds the HTML
the source's renderer writes for test strings written for this sample. No picture or text of a
benchmark is in this tree: the check mode reads pictures that a computer copies to the phone.
